    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d212">

                <pb facs="0510" n="414" sameAs="frus:frus1879/pg414"/>

                <head>No. 191.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Welsh to Mr. Evarts.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1879-03-18"><hi rendition="#italic">March</hi> 18, 1879</date>.
                        (Received March 29.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 247.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have great pleasure in complying with the
                    request of J. R. Hind, esq., F. R. S. and F. R. A. S., foreign secretary of the
                    Royal Astronical Society, expressed in a letter to the secretary of this
                    legation, a copy of which is herewith inclosed, and to send by the dispatch-bag
                    to-day the box stated to contain the gold medal therein mentioned.</p>
                <p>I presume that the society have already communicated in a more formal way to
                    Professor Hall their courteous action in this matter.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>JOHN WELSH.</signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d212-a1.xml" xpointer="d212-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
